{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795820475,"nonce":"i6FfsYtwDrTF6G4HHqeMLRNi+cA=","title":"A stateful ignores layout changes its callback makes on a pointer state change","message":"A `stateful::\u003cButtonState\u003e()` whose callback gives a child `.w(80)` when idle\nand `.w(120)` when hovered stays 80 wide under the pointer, while a color\nchange in the same callback shows.\n\nThe event-driven refresh queues every child update as `RebuildKind::Visual`,\nwhich does not write layout styles or change the child list. The refresh that a\nsignal dependency triggers compares hashes and picks a layout or structural\nrebuild, so the same callback behaves differently by what woke it.\n\nReproduced in a headless session while writing the test for fe2c10c.","files":null}]}